    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f9b7a67_81cb6bd9",
        "filename": "board/atlas_ish/ec.tasklist",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137654
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-04T21:17:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe we should provide 32 bit opaque parameter for a task. Using this parameter to micro-control low level components is not a good idea. We also many task declaration with \"NULL\"(which implicitly indicates word size available) in many ec.tasklist files.\n\nCurrently we have \"name\", \"routine\", \"opaque parameter\", and \"stack size\" in task declaration and among them, \"opaque parameter\" is the only thing should be completely owned by the task and shouldn\u0027t be used by any other components.\n\nWe may use \"name\" with special pre/post-fix or \"routine\"(or \"stack size\") with special least significant bit. I believe we should use \"routine\" or \"stack size\".\n\nMaybe \"routine\" is better than \"stack size\" ? to indicate the task has special property ?\n\n\n\nFor the \"define\", I\u0027ve already defined flag in task.c. I\u0027ll use them in the example.",
      "parentUuid": "74a854fe_0c89fe81",
      "revId": "a99127dcdec3c10b4238c9258028b9e66ba5e272",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b2850fe9_970f0d72",
        "filename": "board/atlas_ish/ec.tasklist",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137654
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-04T22:03:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hm.... I see problem that the values defined here also used by \"util/export_taskinfo.c\". stack_size will be wrong here unless we change this file. I don\u0027t know who is using this but to avoid changing this file, maybe we can introduce new macro for flag(or property) here which can make people easily get what they have to do and provide correct information to other common functions like \"export_taskinfo.c\". for example.\n\n#define MIA_TASK_FLAG_USE_FPU\n#define ROUTINE(r, f)        (r)\n\ndefine CONFIG_TASK_LIST \\\n\tTASK_ALWAYS(HOOKS, ROUTINE(hook_task, 0), NULL, HUGE_TASK_STACK_SIZE) \\\n\tTASK_ALWAYS(FPU_TASK, ROUTINE(fpu_task, MIA_TASK_FLAG_USE_FPU), NULL, LARGER_TASK_STACK_SIZE) \n\nand redefine ROUTINE(r, f) and MIA_TASK_FLAG_USE_FPU in \"task.c\" to get correct information.\n\n\nOR, just use different defines\n\n#define ROUTINE(r)               (r)\n#define ROUTINE_FPU(r)           (r)   \u003c\u003d redefine in task.c\" \n\nAny thought ?",
      "parentUuid": "9f9b7a67_81cb6bd9",
      "revId": "a99127dcdec3c10b4238c9258028b9e66ba5e272",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
